WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.150
Through telescopes, astronomers see dark spots on the Sun's face: sunspots.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.950
They have counted them for centuries, year after year.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.570
Then, in the old records, something strange.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.710
The spots almost vanish.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.170
Decade after decade, hardly any at all.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:26.550
And at roughly the same time, north-west Europe was most likely living through its coldest century for a thousand years.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.710
Missing sunspots, and a freezing Europe, together.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.730
Did the Sun go quiet?

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:38.790
In this mission, you'll read the old sunspot records for yourself, and learn what a correlation is.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.730
You'll meet the author of Frankenstein, and learn to tell evidence from interpretation.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.230
Your mission: decide whether the Sun went quiet.
